TWO CLASS-OF-ERROR FIXES, both the same shape — I had been tuning a parameter
when the structure was wrong:

1. Club text colour, 6 attempts. Every prior attempt picked a different colour
   to tint the text with. The note said 'text color' each time. The answer was
   to stop colouring text at all; the per-card assortment now lives entirely on
   the bar, border and underline.

2. Beams darkening the particle name, 3 attempts. Every prior attempt lowered
   opacity (0.5 -> 0.42 -> 0.28). SideRays was rendered with overlay=z-index:30,
   i.e. painting ON TOP of the name and the hero copy. Dropping overlay put it
   at z-index:0 and the opacity went back UP to 0.40.

The generalisable rule, and it is the same one from pass 13 stated better:
when repeated tuning does not satisfy a note, the note is not about the value.
Find the structural fact — a stacking context, a paint order, a category
decision like 'should this be coloured at all' — and change that instead.

Also: enlarging the wheel while narrowing its column only worked once the
counter/hint pocket stopped being absolute-positioned slack, because until then
'bigger cards' and 'bigger counter' were competing for the same pixels. Two
requirements that seem contradictory usually share one under-specified
resource.
